;; COMPILE-WITH[--hardware-profile=smem162e]: FAIL "exceeding the hardware profile"
;; SKIP-DEFAULT-PASS
;;   The refusal REQUIRES an active profile: with none selected there is no shared-memory bound
;;   to exceed and this kernel compiles perfectly well.  So it is a COMPILE-WITH...FAIL spec
;;   rather than an errors/ rung -- errors/ specs must fail in the flagless Default pass, and
;;   opting one out with SKIP-DEFAULT-PASS makes it vacuously "pass", which the runner correctly
;;   reports as "Test passed but was expected to fail".  Same idiom as
;;   133-mma-spv/13-col-major-operand-refused-bmg, whose refusal also needs a profile selected.
;;
;; THE TILE IS DELIBERATELY UNUSED, and that is not a weakness of the test.  What the profile
;; bound check counts -- and what the launcher actually reserves -- is the DECLARED scratch
;; signature, not what the body reads back.  Verified directly: the same tile under a 50KB cap
;; is refused with "uses 65536 bytes", which is 32,768 x 2, so the declaration alone exercises
;; both the width table and the check.  Keeping the body trivial also keeps the rung about ONE
;; thing; a read-back would drag element conversion into a spec that is not about conversion.
;; Endeavour 162 — the CONTROL: widening 16-bit must not widen everything.
;;
;; This is the same 256 x 128 = 32,768-element tile as rung 01, in `float` instead of bfloat16.
;; At 4 bytes it is 131,072 bytes against a 100KB (102,400) cap, so it MUST still be refused.
;;
;; WHY THIS RUNG EXISTS.  Rung 01 alone is satisfied by a table that returns 2 for EVERYTHING --
;; which would under-reserve every 32-bit kernel in the tree and corrupt their shared layouts,
;; the failure mode BUG 046 was about (sizer and emitters disagreeing).  A test that a fix can
;; satisfy by being wrong in the other direction is not a test of the fix.  Together the two
;; rungs pin the RELATIONSHIP -- 16-bit is half of 32-bit -- rather than either number alone.
;;
;; It also guards the bound check itself: if %hp-check-shared-memory ever stops running, this
;; rung compiles clean and says so.
(declaim (precision fast))
(def-hardware-profile smem162e
  :simd-width 32
  :max-shared-memory-per-block 100KB)
(def-type mt (matrix float :address-space :global :align :compact :contiguous-term :row-major))
(def-kernel float_scratch_too_big (&out C)
  (declare #'(&out mt) (global-size :set-to 128) (local-size :set-to 128))
  (let ((tile (make-scratch-matrix float (256 128))))
    (set! (~ C 0 0) 1.0)))
